L224: To a solution of **4** (6.9g, 15.6 mmol) in dry THF (50ml), lithium aluminum hydride (1.18g, 31.2
L225: mmol) was added in two batches at 0°C under a nitrogen atmosphere. After 3.5h, the reaction
L226: mixture was diluted with DCM and quenched slowly with water and then brought to pH 6-7 with
L227: 1M HCl. (Note: Prolonged exposure to acidic conditions leads to dimerization of 6-HMTC.) The
L228: phases were separated, and the water phase was washed 5x with CH2Cl2. The organic phases
L229: were combined and dried over Na2SO4 and dried down to dryness. Silica column
L230: chromatography (CH2Cl2 to CH2Cl2/MeOH 50:1) afforded 4 (6.9g, 97.7%) as a clear oil.
