L239: **Supplementary Material** _**2: Nuclear receptor assays.**_ To examine the possibility that vitamin
L240: E modulates gene expression through impacting hormone nuclear receptors, we employed
L241: specific reporter assays. In each case, we transfected cultured cells with expression vector for
L242: the nuclear receptor, alongside a reporter construct in which expression of the firefly luciferase
L243: is driven by the appropriate response element using Lipofectamine 2000 (Invitrogen, Carlsbad,
L244: CA). After 24 hours, an appropriate ligand (positive control, tocopherol, or solvent control) was
L245: added, and luminescence was measured using the Dual glow Luciferase Assay (Promega) in a
L246: Tecan Spark plate reader. Firefly luminescence was normalized to that of Renilla (cotransfected in the pRL-TK vector). Transfections were done in 4-9 replicates in 96-well plates
L247: using 120 ng of luciferase reporter construct, 30 ng of receptor expression vector, and 15 ng of
L248: the Renilla pRL-TK plasmid. In each case, a-tocopherol was added from an ethanolic stock, as
L249: well as a lipoprotein-bound complex prepared as described earlier (80). Reagent combinations
L250: for each nuclear receptor are provided in the Table below as well as representative data.
